{"name":"Crazy Eyes","hex":"#5eb68d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crazy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of unsound mind; insane; demented. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Out of control."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very, extremely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crazy"},{"term":"eyes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of eye"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of eye"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crazy Eyes","blocks":[{"text":"Crazy Eyes is the fifth studio album released by the American country rock band Poco. Released in 1973, Crazy Eyes was the band's final album with founding member Richie Furay during his original tenure in Poco."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a1/POCO_CRAZY_EYES.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Eyes"},{"title":"Crazy Eyes (Orange Is the New Black)","blocks":[{"text":"Suzanne \"Crazy Eyes\" Warren is a fictional character played by Uzo Aduba on the Netflix series Orange Is the New Black. Warren is portrayed as intelligent and creative, but lacking in social skills and prone to spiral into emotional, sometimes violent, outbursts and delusions when agitated due to mental illness. She is a recurring character in season one and a regular character beginning with season two."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Crazy_Eyes_%28OITNB%2C_season_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Eyes_(Orange_Is_the_New_Black)"},{"title":"Insanity","blocks":[{"text":"Insanity, madness, lunacy, moon-addled, and craziness are behaviors caused by certain abnormal mental or behavioral patterns. Insanity can manifest as violations of societal norms, including a person or persons becoming a danger to themselves or to other people. Conceptually, mental insanity also is associated with the biological phenomenon of contagion as in the case of copycat suicides. In contemporary usage, the term insanity is an informal, un-scientific term denoting \"mental instability\"; thus, the term insanity defense is the legal definition of mental instability. In medicine, the general term psychosis is used to include the presence of delusions or hallucinations in a patient; and psychiatric illness is \"psychopathology\", not mental insanity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/The_Rake%27s_Progress_8.jpg/330px-The_Rake%27s_Progress_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insanity"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Casa_de_locos.jpg/500px-Casa_de_locos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Casa_de_locos.jpg/500px-Casa_de_locos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goya's Madhouse, 1812-1819","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACasa_de_locos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg/500px-Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg/500px-Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eye of a European bison","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg/500px-%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg/1280px-%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg/500px-%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human eye","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Odontodactylus_scyllarus_eyes.jpg/500px-Odontodactylus_scyllarus_eyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Odontodactylus_scyllarus_eyes.jpg/1280px-Odontodactylus_scyllarus_eyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Odontodactylus_scyllarus_eyes.jpg/500px-Odontodactylus_scyllarus_eyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The eyes of a mantis shrimp (here O